  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DSB 2024: General support</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">General support. The Directorate for Civil Protection (DSB) collaborates with the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and the Ministry of Justice on international affairs. In this collaboration, DSB manages tasks related to humanitarian work, medical evacuation (Medevac) to Ukraine, Gaza, etc., in-kind assistance via the EU, Civil Preparedness Mechanism (UCPM) to Ukraine and Moldova and other countries when the UCPM mechanism is activated, and climate and environmental activities. DSB is point of contact to the EU, UN, and NATO civilian crisis management mechanisms. DSB also oversee the main concepts for international operational activities for humanitarian efforts, involving Norwegian UNDAC Support (NUS), Norwegian Support Team (NST), UNDAC experts, EU experts, and Medevac experts, as well as other liaisons. The task includes personnel management, including capacity building and recruitment, updating and maintenance of equipment and cooperation with relevant partners through established cooperation forums and support for development work and course activities for international organizations</narrative>
  </description>
